# Vendor-export drop directory (handoff 0015 adapters, Path C of
# docs/connecting-your-data.md). Drop your vendor system's own export
# files here — e.g. a TripSpark Streets APC CSV — and the ingestion
# service picks them up within about half a minute, moving handled files
# into processed/.
#
# Agency operational data, never source: nothing in here is committed.
#
# THIS .gitignore IS TRACKED ON PURPOSE, so the directory exists in every
# checkout. Without it, Docker creates the bind-mount path itself on first
# `up` — owned by ROOT — and the person who then tries to copy an export
# in gets permission denied for reasons that have nothing to do with them.
# A tracked placeholder means the folder belongs to whoever cloned the
# repo. (Same lesson as the 2026-07-28 nginx file-mode incident: never let
# a host permission accident decide whether the product works.)
*
!.gitignore
